// Luxy foundational conversation and execution rules.
! version = 2.0
! var name = Luxy

+ intent chat greet
* <get greeted> == yes => {@welcome back}
- <set greeted=yes>Hello! What would you like to explore?{weight=2}
- <set greeted=yes>Hi, I’m Luxy. What can I help you find?
- <set greeted=yes>Welcome to Luxraj Blog!

+ intent chat thanks
- You’re welcome. Happy reading!
- Glad I could help.
- Anytime. What else would you like to explore?

+ intent chat farewell
- See you around!
- Take care, and thanks for visiting.
- Until next time!

+ intent chat smalltalk
- I’m ready to help you explore the blog. What are you curious about?
- Doing well, thanks for asking!

+ intent assistant identity
- I’m <bot name>, the search assistant for Luxraj Blog. I can help you find articles, follow sources and use site controls.

+ intent assistant help
- Try asking for articles on a topic, a blog section, the author of the current article, or the light theme. I can show relevant excerpts and link you to their sources.

+ intent site identity
- Luxraj Blog is an editorial publication covering engineering, electronics, computing and practical technology. The About page has the full story. <call>about</call>

+ intent site creator
- Luxraj Kayal created and maintains Luxraj Blog. He publishes under the name Luxraj. <call>about</call>

+ intent newsletter info
- The Luxraj Blog newsletter is an email subscription. You can review the signup form in Luxy’s Cottage or use the unsubscribe page to leave the list.

+ welcome back
- Welcome back! What would you like to look up this time?

+ intent site navigate
* <get missing> == page => {@outcome clarify page}
- <call>navigate</call>

+ intent site contact
- <call>contact</call>

+ intent site theme
- <call>theme</call>

+ intent site language
* <get missing> == language => {@outcome clarify language}
- <call>language</call>

+ intent search interface
- <call>search_interface</call>

+ intent newsletter subscribe
- <call>newsletter</call>

+ intent newsletter unsubscribe
- <call>unsubscribe</call>

+ intent article share
- <call>share</call>

+ intent article copylink
- <call>copy</call>

+ intent article author
- <call>author</call>

+ intent article date
- <call>article_dates</call>

+ intent article calculate
* <get missing> == expression => {@outcome clarify expression}
- <call>calculate</call>

+ intent content explain
* <get missing> == query => {@outcome clarify query}
- <call>retrieve</call>

+ intent content search
- <call>retrieve</call>

+ intent content category
- <call>category</call>

+ intent content author
* <get missing> == author => {@outcome clarify author}
- <call>retrieve</call>

+ intent content date
- <call>retrieve</call>

+ intent content more
* <get hasrelated> == yes => <call>retrieve</call>
* <get missing> == query => {@outcome clarify query}
- <call>retrieve</call>

+ intent content refine
* <get missing> == query => {@outcome clarify query}
- <call>retrieve</call>

+ outcome unavailable
- I can’t open that here. Try another section or ask for a topic.

+ outcome error
- Something went wrong while I was working on that. Please try again.

+ outcome destination
- Here’s the page you can open.

+ outcome categories
- Here are the available sections.

+ outcome language unavailable
- I couldn’t find a published home page for that language.

+ outcome theme light
- The site is now using the light theme.

+ outcome theme dark
- The site is now using the dark theme.

+ outcome opened
- I opened the requested search controls.

+ outcome offer newsletter
- Open the signup form to review it and subscribe through the newsletter service.

+ outcome newsletter opened
- The newsletter form is open. Follow the instructions there to subscribe.

+ outcome offer share
- Use your device’s share options, or copy the article link.

+ outcome offer copy
- Use the button to copy this article’s link.

+ outcome copy manually
- Automatic copying is unavailable. You can open the link and copy it from the address bar.

+ outcome copied
- The article link was copied.

+ outcome shared
- Your device accepted the share request.

+ outcome share cancelled
- Sharing was cancelled.

+ outcome article needed
- Open an article first so I know which page you mean.

+ outcome author
- Here’s the byline for this article.

+ outcome author unavailable
- I couldn’t find a confirmed byline for this article.

+ outcome article dates
- Here are the dates recorded for this article.

+ outcome calculator unavailable
- This article doesn’t currently have a calculation tool I can use.

+ outcome calculated
- The article’s calculator returned this result.

+ outcome date unavailable
- The requested date information is unavailable here.

+ outcome local index unavailable
- I couldn’t find a published search index for this language.

+ outcome found
- I found these results on Luxraj Blog.

+ outcome explained
- These excerpts from Luxraj Blog may help explain the topic. Open a source to read more.

+ outcome empty
- I didn’t find matching pages. Try a different term or a broader topic.

+ outcome exhausted
- There are no more matching results from this search.

+ outcome clarify query
- Which topic should I look up?

+ outcome clarify page
- Which page would you like to open?

+ outcome clarify language
- Which language version would you like to open?

+ outcome clarify author
- Which author should I look for?

+ outcome clarify expression
- What values or expression should the article tool use?

+ notice unfiltered
- Some requested filters weren’t available in the website index.

+ label offer newsletter
- Open newsletter

+ label offer share
- Share article

+ label offer copy
- Copy link

+ label published
- Published

+ label modified
- Updated

+ unknown
- {topic=recovery}I didn’t understand that request. Try naming a topic, a blog section or a site control.

+ ambiguous
- {topic=recovery}I’m not sure what you’re referring to. Could you name the article, topic or control?

+ *
- {@unknown}

> topic recovery includes random
+ intent assistant help
- {topic=random}Try asking for articles on a topic, a blog section, the author of the current article, or the light theme. I can show relevant excerpts and link you to their sources.
< topic
